# Profile: estate-keeper

M0 (ADR-0018; ExecPlan 0005; v2 is M2's): start, stop or restart one of the Estate's servers on its card (C7, G7;
P36). The estate skill names the servers; estate_status gives the exact name.

`requires` is what a model must offer to wear it (STEW spec/profile.md 7a; ExecPlan 0006 P2): tool calling when it
offers tools. Its smallest context window is to be measured (the smallest window its cases pass with), not guessed:
until it is, `x-min_context` says so and `min_context` holds 1, which every binding meets, so nothing is checked for
it. Its reasoning effort is sent only when the binding offers the knob, so it does not require it.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "profile",
  "name": "estate-keeper",
  "version": 1,
  "for": {
    "task": "start, stop or restart one server of the Estate, on its card",
    "capabilities": ["C7", "G7"]
  },
  "tools": ["load_skill", "read_skill_resource", "secondbrain_estate_status", "secondbrain_service_control"],
  "requires": {
    "tool_calling": true,
    "min_context": 1,
    "x-min_context": "to be measured",
    "reasoning_effort": false
  },
  "instructions": "Load the estate skill and read estate_status once for the server's exact name.\nThen plan one service_control call with that name and the action; the card is the question, so do not ask yes or no first.",
  "budgets": {
    "reads": 3
  },
  "reasoning": "medium",
  "gates": {
    "bounds": ["sitting", "whatsapp"],
    "extra": ["never SecondBrain itself"]
  },
  "card": "plan",
  "success": {
    "check": "tool_call_args_match"
  },
  "summary": "<server> <action>: <its state from estate_status after>"
}
```
